/-!
# Immersions between regular schemes

An immersion `i : Z ⟶ X` of schemes whose source and target are both regular is a regular
immersion.  At a point `z` of `Z` the map of local rings `O_{X, i z} ⟶ O_{Z, z}` is a surjection
between regular local rings, so its kernel is generated by a regular sequence; over a locally
Noetherian target that condition at every point is regularity of the immersion.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isRegularImmersion_of_isRegular`: an immersion
  between regular schemes is a regular immersion.

## Implementation notes

Both regularity hypotheses are used through `AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_tfae`, which reads
regularity of a scheme as local Noetherianity together with regularity of every local ring.  Local
Noetherianity of the target is the hypothesis of the stalkwise criterion
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isRegularImmersion_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap`,
and regularity of the two local rings is what makes the kernel of their surjection regular.

The statement about local rings is the case `A → B → B` of
`IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isRegular_ker_tfae`:  with the second map the identity its kernel is
the zero ideal, which the empty sequence generates regularly, so the equivalence returns a regular
sequence generating the kernel of the first map.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.12 (Tag 0E9J)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E9J)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.21.8 (Tag 063I)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063I)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 10.106.3 (Tag 00NQ)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NQ)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 10.106.4 (Tag 00NR)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NR)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

universe u

/-- **The kernel of a surjection of regular local rings is generated by a regular sequence.**
The quotient of a regular local ring by the ideal is again regular local, which pins the minimal
number of generators of that ideal to the drop in dimension. -/
private theorem exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_ker {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing B] {f : A →+* B} (hf : Function.Surjective f) :
    ∃ rs : List A, RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular A rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker f := by
  have htfae := (IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isRegular_ker_tfae (f := f) (g := RingHom.id B)
    hf Function.surjective_id).out 3 1
  have hker : Ideal.ofList ([] : List B) = RingHom.ker (RingHom.id B) := by
    ext b; simp [RingHom.mem_ker]
  obtain ⟨rs, hreg, hspan⟩ := htfae.mp ⟨[], RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular.nil B B, hker⟩
  exact ⟨rs, hreg, by simpa using hspan⟩

/-- **Stacks tag 0E9J.** An immersion between regular schemes is a regular immersion. -/
@[stacks 0E9J, ega "IV 19.7.5" "more general"]
theorem isRegularImmersion_of_isRegular {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (hZ : AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular Z) (hX : AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X) :
    IsRegularImmersion i := by
  obtain ⟨hNoethX, hstalkX⟩ := ((AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_tfae X).out 1 2).mp hX
  obtain ⟨-, hstalkZ⟩ := ((AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_tfae Z).out 1 2).mp hZ
  have _ : IsLocallyNoetherian X := hNoethX
  refine isRegularImmersion_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap i fun z => ?_
  have _ : IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)) := hstalkX (i.base z)
  have _ : IsRegularLocalRing (Z.presheaf.stalk z) := hstalkZ z
  exact exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_ker (f := (i.stalkMap z).hom) (i.stalkMap_surjective z)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

end
